cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Triplet energy transfer kinetics — data, benchmarks and models
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or code, please cite both this repository and the
  accompanying paper.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Niklas
    family-names: Hölter
  - given-names: Leon
    family-names: Schlosser
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/
abstract: >-
  Automated Stern–Volmer quenching data for 27 photocatalysts against 48
  quenchers in acetonitrile (1296 pairs), the DFT and molecular-dynamics
  calculations describing them, and the scripts that turn instrument output
  into the tables used in the paper. Includes benchmarks of adiabatic, Marcus,
  Rehm–Weller and DvTE treatments as classifiers of triplet energy transfer.
keywords:
  - triplet energy transfer
  - photocatalysis
  - Stern-Volmer
  - Marcus theory
  - machine learning
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: software
    title: pyRates — prediction of energy transfer kinetics
    authors:
      - given-names: Leon
        family-names: Schlosser
    repository-code: https://github.com/le-schlo/pyrates
    license: MIT
